In-Reply-To: <4wwEW9fMm3w.RK8v3C6zrQUJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
References: <4wwEW9fMm3w.RK8v3C6zrQUJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/deducer/c/4wwEW9fMm3w/m/FQotH6Gk6BMJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

You can do that with the function xtabs. It's not included among Deducer dialogs, but it's fairly easy to use. If your data frame DF has the variables "organism", "status", and "freq", just type:

xtabs(freq~organism+status, data=DF)

Helios

